--TEST--
A written-out `propertyPath<T>` with a part that names no public property, or that continues after a property that is not an object, is the unknown-member error at that part alone, with `as` and at a parameter — `rule:types/property-path`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Each part of a path is checked when the program compiles.
class Customer {
    public string $name = "Ada";
    private string $secret = "s";
}

class Order {
    public ?Customer $customer = null;
    public int $total = 40;
}

class Report {
    public static function column(propertyPath<Order> $path): string {
        return "column " . ($path as string);
    }
}

// `nmae` is misspelled.
echo "customer.nmae" as propertyPath<Order> as string, "\n";
// `secret` is private.
echo Report::column("customer.secret"), "\n";
// `total` is an `int`, so the path cannot continue after it.
echo Report::column("total.amount"), "\n";
// A path that ends with a dot has an empty last part.
echo Report::column("customer."), "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0405]: `Customer` has no public property `$nmae`
   --> %s:20:16
   |
20 | echo "customer.nmae" as propertyPath<Order> as string, "\n";
   |                ^^^^ this part of the path is checked here
   = help: each part of a property path names a public property of the class the path has reached: `Customer` has `$name`

error[E0405]: `Customer` has no public property `$secret`
   --> %s:22:31
   |
22 | echo Report::column("customer.secret"), "\n";
   |                               ^^^^^^ this part of the path is checked here
   = help: each part of a property path names a public property of the class the path has reached: `Customer` has `$name`

error[E0405]: `Order`'s property `$total` is not an object, so the path cannot continue after it
   --> %s:24:22
   |
24 | echo Report::column("total.amount"), "\n";
   |                      ^^^^^ the path continues after this property
   = help: every part of a property path but the last names a property whose type is a class, a nullable class or an array of a class

error[E0405]: a property path has an empty part
   --> %s:26:21
   |
26 | echo Report::column("customer."), "\n";
   |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^ this path is checked here
   = help: a property path is property names joined with one dot, such as `customer.name`

error: aborting due to 4 errors
